Spawning stock biomass (B) is always female in our rockfish models (to date). However, the harvest rate u=Catch/VB is catch over vulnerable biomass (males and females). We don't typically report VB, although we do calculate a VB in MPD|MCMC output. However, VB is specific to a gear|fleet and if there is more than one gear|fleet, the output VB per gear|fleet is not additive because it's the portion of total biomass that is vulnerable by each gear|fleet (through selectivity). Sometimes a 'harvest rate fraction' is used to prorate u (e.g., 0.95 trawl and 0.05 hook & line) to derive a single VB.
 
